\f2\ltrch\u10022?\f1\lang1033  Integrating Single Sign-On (SSO) across three independent projects\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 (questionretrieval, online-exam, and newboard) is a significant architectural\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 move. Based on your current structure (FastAPI backends, JWT authentication, and\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 MySQL/SQLite databases), here is the most practical path forward:\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 1. The Strategy: Centralized Authentication Server (Identity Provider)\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Instead of trying to sync three separate databases, you should designate one\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 project (or create a new, lightweight service) as the Central Identity Provider\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 (IdP).\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * How it works:\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
       \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * When a user logs in, they go to the Central IdP.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
       \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * The IdP validates credentials against your central user table.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
       \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * Upon success, it issues a signed JWT that is shared (via domain cookies or\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
         \f1\ltrch\lang1033 a redirect URL) with the other two applications.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
       \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * Each app trusts the signature of the Central IdP using the same\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
         \f1\ltrch\lang1033 SECRET_KEY.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 2. Immediate Integration Steps (Architectural)\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 To move in this direction, follow these steps:\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 A. Centralize User Data\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Decide which database will hold the "Master" user table. Currently, it seems\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 newboard and online-exam might have different user stores. You must create a\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 shared table or a shared authentication microservice.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 B. Unified Token Validation\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Currently, your backend/core/security.py uses settings.SECRET_KEY and\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 settings.ALGORITHM. For SSO to work:\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * Synchronize Configuration: All three projects must use the exact same\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
     \f1\ltrch\lang1033 SECRET_KEY and ALGORITHM in their .env files.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * Shared Token Schema: Ensure that when newboard creates a token, online-exam\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
     \f1\ltrch\lang1033 can read the sub (subject/user ID) and role claims from that same token.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 C. Cross-App Redirects\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 When a user logs into newboard, they receive a cookie. If you set the domain of\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 that cookie to .yourdomain.com (e.g., .tams.com), the cookie will automatically\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 be sent when the user navigates to online-exam.yourdomain.com. The backend of\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 online-exam then just needs to validate that incoming JWT.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 3. Recommendation\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Do not rewrite all three apps. Start by:\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 1. Identifying which app will be your "Login Portal".\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 2. Ensuring all three apps share the same SECRET_KEY.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 3. Implementing a middleware in online-exam and questionretrieval that accepts a\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
      \f1\ltrch\lang1033 JWT from newboard.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Do you have a common domain for these three projects (e.g., app1.yoursite.com,\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 app2.yoursite.com)? If so, I can provide the exact middleware code to validate\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 cross-application tokens.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
