  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Here is the architectural plan to make your lms-platform-frontend the entry point\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 and have the three backends (newboard, online-exam, question-retrieval) share the\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 same authentication state.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 1. The Core Strategy: Shared JWT Validation\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Since all your backends are using FastAPI, we will rely on JWT (JSON Web Tokens).\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * Central Login: Your lms-platform-frontend (the entry point) will send user\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
     \f1\ltrch\lang1033 credentials to a Central Auth API.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * Token Issuance: Upon successful login, the Central Auth API issues a JWT\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
     \f1\ltrch\lang1033 containing user claims (e.g., user_id, role, tenant_id).\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * Universal Secret: You must copy the exact same SECRET_KEY and ALGORITHM from\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
     \f1\ltrch\lang1033 your central auth settings into the .env files of all three backend projects.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * Universal Validation: Any request to online-exam, dashboard, or\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
     \f1\ltrch\lang1033 question-retrieval will now contain this JWT. Each backend will use its own\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
     \f1\ltrch\lang1033 copy of the SECRET_KEY to verify the token signature. If the signature\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
     \f1\ltrch\lang1033 matches, the user is automatically "logged in" to that specific app.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  ---\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 2. Implementation Steps\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Step 1: Centralize Authentication\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Choose one backend (or create a new shared auth-service) to be the Identity\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Provider (IdP).\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * This service will handle: /login, /register, /token/verify.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * Update your security.py in all three projects so the code used to verify\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
     \f1\ltrch\lang1033 tokens is identical.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Step 2: Configure Shared Security\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Open backend/core/config.py (or your .env files) in all three projects and ensure\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 they use these exact same variables:\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 1 # Shared Security Config\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 2 SECRET_KEY="your-ultra-secret-shared-key"\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 3 ALGORITHM="HS256"\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Step 3: Configure Shared Cookies (The "Invisible Login")\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 To make the login seamless, you should set the JWT in a cookie that is readable\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 across your subdomains:\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 * In your login logic, set the cookie domain to your parent domain:\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 1     response.set_cookie(\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 2         key="access_token",\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 3         value=token,\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 4         domain=".yourdomain.com",  # This allows subdomains to share it\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 5         httponly=True,\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   \f1\ltrch\lang1033 6         secure=True\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
   7     )\par
\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Step 4: Middleware Update\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 In all three backends, update your authentication dependency (typically\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 Depends(get_current_user)) to simply read the access_token from the cookie and\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
  \f1\ltrch\lang1033 decode it using the shared SECRET_KEY.\f0\rtlch\lang1025\par
\par
  ---\par
